WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.094
Performance decisions sit within larger systems.

2
00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:05.906
Compensation includes pay and benefits.

3
00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:14.310
Internal equity compares pay relationships within an organization; external equity compares relevant work in other organizations.

4
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:18.922
A manager's recommendation for a raise is not the same as an approved award.

5
00:00:19.122 --> 00:00:21.851
Funding, pay structures, and authority matter.

6
00:00:22.051 --> 00:00:26.814
Discipline addresses conduct or performance problems under applicable procedures.

7
00:00:27.014 --> 00:00:32.323
It should be consistent, based on relevant facts, and directed toward correction where appropriate.

8
00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:40.810
The steps and available actions depend on the situation and the institution; there is no universal ladder that every incident must follow.

9
00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:47.201
A grievance procedure gives an employee a defined way to raise and seek review of a workplace complaint.

10
00:00:47.401 --> 00:00:51.477
Using that process is not itself proof of wrongdoing by either side.

11
00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:57.968
Do not confuse a coaching conversation with formal discipline or a disagreement with a completed grievance.

12
00:00:58.168 --> 00:01:05.850
The diagram keeps these routes separate while connecting each to clear expectations, evidence, authorized decisions, and follow-through.
